package CanvasNet {
    part def ScadGeometryBuilder {
        /* cspell:ignore minkowski */
        doc /* The internal ScadGeometryBuilder engine (a sealed partial class) and its supporting types that convert the instantiation tree of an evaluation into a Render3D scene: an iterative post-order walk over an explicit stack (no recursion anywhere in the Geometry namespace, so any caller stack works), the implicit union of groups, loops, and user modules, dispatch tables for leaf, container, and unsupported modules (text, offset, projection, surface, import, and roof are reported as scad-module-{name} and omitted, while a user module of the same name shadows the built-in), the show-only, highlight, and background modifiers, the position-preserving difference, the intersection, and the mixed 2D and 3D rules of the CSG booleans (ScadBooleans) with bounds for resize, the hull and minkowski convex combinations (ScadHulls: the exact hull of the points of 3D or 2D children, and the Minkowski sum of convex 3D children folded from the left with unions distributed, built on the Render3D ConvexHull and MinkowskiSum units, with the scad-hull-* and scad-minkowski-* reports for booleans, non-convex, mixed-dimension, degenerate, deferred 2D, and too-complex operands), top-level 2D shapes as slabs of the flat-shape thickness, a triangle budget charged before allocation (the exact count for primitives and extrusions; an upper bound of 2d - 4 for a hull and 2 * Va * Vb - 4 for each Minkowski sum, plus the transformed copies of the convex parts, settled to the exact count or refunded afterwards) and failing with a located ScadEvaluationException, cancellation polling, one reporting channel into the evaluation's sink with strict-mode ScadUnsupportedFeatureException and de-duplicated, file-aware locations, the map from mesh nodes to source locations, and the copy of the renderer options with a substituted handler and the render3d- to scad- feature identifier mapping. */

